WEBVTT

00:06.110 --> 00:08.940
A massive horde 
of monsters heading for Valmer?

00:08.940 --> 00:11.740
Don't tell me... Could this be a flood?

00:11.740 --> 00:12.820
A flood?

00:12.820 --> 00:13.360
Yeah.

00:13.740 --> 00:17.370
When the magic matter overflowing from
a holy land coalesces enough,

00:17.700 --> 00:20.450
it transforms, released as monsters.

00:21.080 --> 00:23.500
We call that a flood.

00:24.170 --> 00:26.920
<i>Looks like most of them are low-level.</i>

00:27.750 --> 00:29.880
Why have they set their sights on Valmer?

00:29.880 --> 00:34.010
The area around the holy land 
is protected by Mist Garuda.

00:34.010 --> 00:36.800
The only path to avoid
 it is the road to Valmer.

00:37.240 --> 00:42.100
Which is why Valmer is fortified. 
It serves as a bulwark against such floods.

00:42.100 --> 00:46.270
I see. So they're equipped
 to fend these things off, huh?

00:46.270 --> 00:47.310
No.

00:47.610 --> 00:51.150
There are strong soldiers 
and chosen ones in Valmer, yes,

00:51.150 --> 00:55.100
but the city always suffers
 significant casualties.

00:55.100 --> 00:58.200
And up against a major flood like this...

00:58.660 --> 01:01.410
<i>I should have Schnee hurry, just in case.</i>

01:02.040 --> 01:05.120
There's still time before the
 monsters reach Valmer.

01:05.120 --> 01:06.710
We'll hurry there and join the guard.

01:06.710 --> 01:07.580
Shin?

01:07.580 --> 01:11.250
I can't just say "so long, nice knowin' ya"
 given the circumstances.

01:12.420 --> 01:13.340
Got it.

01:18.830 --> 01:20.670
So this is Valmer, huh?

01:20.670 --> 01:23.720
Shin, how long until the monsters arrive?

01:24.140 --> 01:26.890
Probably a few days, I'd say.

01:26.890 --> 01:29.860
I see. I'm going to meet with the local lord.

01:30.360 --> 01:33.230
You make your report to the adventurer's guild.

01:33.230 --> 01:34.490
What about after that?

01:34.820 --> 01:39.700
The guild and the army will be essential 
to counter a large-scale invasion.

01:39.700 --> 01:42.030
The chosen ones will gather first thing.

01:42.030 --> 01:43.740
Okay, got it.

01:45.080 --> 01:47.250
Welcome to the adventurer's guild.

01:47.670 --> 01:50.630
I'm the guildmaster, Baron Lakt.

01:51.040 --> 01:52.580
My name's Shin.

01:52.580 --> 01:53.800
Shin, eh?

01:53.800 --> 01:56.130
I heard you have information about the flood.

01:56.470 --> 01:58.930
Yes. A flood of primarily humanoid monsters

01:58.930 --> 02:03.630
like goblins and orcs has appeared 
in the vicinity of the Holy Land Calkia.

02:03.630 --> 02:07.850
At the speed they're going, 
they should reach Valmer in a few days.

02:07.850 --> 02:09.020
That soon?

02:09.400 --> 02:11.520
You sound like you've seen it for yourself.

02:11.810 --> 02:15.940
I saw a large number of monsters 
heading towards Valmer near the holy land.

02:15.940 --> 02:16.900
I see.

02:17.400 --> 02:21.120
If that's true, we can begin
 preparing right away, but...

02:21.120 --> 02:24.030
Will this make you believe me?

02:24.950 --> 02:27.040
Is that from the Moon Sanctum?

02:27.320 --> 02:31.500
Yes. If you still don't 
believe me, ask your lord.

02:31.500 --> 02:35.000
My companion is currently 
getting in touch with them.

02:35.000 --> 02:38.170
No, I see now that you aren't lying.

02:38.670 --> 02:41.470
I'm declaring a state of emergency.

02:41.930 --> 02:47.720
If your companion has an audience with
the lord, then the army will act posthaste.

02:47.720 --> 02:51.730
As soon as we get word, 
we'll begin evacuating the citizens.

02:51.730 --> 02:55.270
Eliza, get in touch with 
the representatives of every guild.

02:55.270 --> 02:56.650
Understood.

02:58.990 --> 03:00.700
What will you do now?

03:01.570 --> 03:03.450
Let me lend you my aid.

03:03.820 --> 03:05.530
That'd be a huge boon.

03:05.530 --> 03:08.870
We're short on chosen ones
 to defend the city right now.

03:08.870 --> 03:10.600
Much obliged for the help.

03:10.600 --> 03:11.210
Sure thing.

03:13.670 --> 03:16.590
I should meet back up with Rionne.

03:18.590 --> 03:21.090
I feel like I've seen that before...

03:21.680 --> 03:23.470
"Meow Land"?

03:23.890 --> 03:26.010
Wait, don't tell me this store is...

03:26.010 --> 03:27.180
No, hang on.

03:27.180 --> 03:30.230
<i>Shin, I will be arriving in Valmer shortly.</i>

03:30.230 --> 03:31.980
<i>Got it. Once you're here,</i>

03:31.980 --> 03:35.940
<i>let the lord and guildmaster 
know you'll be joining the defense.</i>

03:35.940 --> 03:37.150
<i>Understood.</i>

03:38.730 --> 03:42.110
<i>Also, I found a curious store in Valmer.</i>

03:42.110 --> 03:44.370
<i>It's called Meow Land.</i>

03:44.370 --> 03:45.450
<i>Have you heard of it?</i>

03:45.450 --> 03:47.490
<i>No. I haven't the faintest idea.</i>

03:47.490 --> 03:49.870
<i>I see.</i>

03:49.870 --> 03:51.960
Thanks for handling the rest.

03:52.510 --> 03:54.000
Y-You...

03:54.000 --> 03:56.670
Is that you, Berett?

03:56.670 --> 03:59.880
Well, well! It's good to see you again, Shin.

04:00.260 --> 04:03.550
I was hoping we'd run 
into each other someday.

04:04.180 --> 04:05.140
Y-Yeah.

04:05.840 --> 04:09.890
<i>I wasn't expecting to run into a friend's
 support character from the game.</i>

04:10.430 --> 04:13.390
<i>But Schnee exists, so I guess it makes sense.</i>

04:14.310 --> 04:17.980
So you'll be helping us turn back the flood?

04:17.980 --> 04:21.400
Yeah. I just finished talking
 to the guildmaster.

04:21.400 --> 04:27.480
I see. But if it's just a flood, couldn't 
you have wiped it out when you found it?

04:28.240 --> 04:31.790
I was with the second princess 
of Bayrelicht at the time.

04:31.790 --> 04:35.580
I can't exactly use my full strength
 with her watching.

04:35.580 --> 04:41.300
I see. High humans these days
are practically revered like gods.

04:41.630 --> 04:43.970
I could see a princess proposing to you.

04:45.180 --> 04:47.930
She's actually interested in me, so I'm trying

04:47.930 --> 04:50.930
to deal with the flood 
without revealing my true strength.

04:50.930 --> 04:55.890
I see. Well, you're an old friend 
of my master's.

04:55.890 --> 04:59.020
If there's any way I can help,
just let me know.

04:59.020 --> 05:00.440
I appreciate it.

05:00.440 --> 05:04.700
Oh, right. I just happened upon
 a shop called Meow Land.

05:05.030 --> 05:08.370
That's your friend Hibineko's shop.

05:08.370 --> 05:09.450
Hibineko?!

05:09.950 --> 05:11.910
Hibineko's here in this world?

05:11.910 --> 05:14.010
You didn't know?

05:14.010 --> 05:16.960
Shadow and Holly are here in Valmer too.

05:17.580 --> 05:18.960
They are?

05:18.960 --> 05:24.880
Yes. They're currently out of the city
on business, but they're doing well.

05:24.880 --> 05:26.090
I see.

05:26.410 --> 05:30.470
<i>I thought all three of them
 died in the death game.</i>

05:31.180 --> 05:32.970
<i>What are they doing in this world?</i>

05:32.970 --> 05:36.140
I didn't expect you to be so surprised.

05:36.140 --> 05:39.360
I have a list of players in this world.

05:39.360 --> 05:40.680
Would you like to see it?

05:40.680 --> 05:42.860
You do? Show me.

05:45.610 --> 05:47.110
This is the whole list?

05:47.110 --> 05:51.370
Yes, though of course
 it's not comprehensive.

05:51.370 --> 05:54.500
<i>Just learning there are other 
former players is a shock.</i>

05:54.500 --> 05:58.870
<i>But all the players living here
were involved with me in some way.</i>

05:58.870 --> 06:00.130
Also...

06:00.750 --> 06:02.290
Take a look at this.

06:03.000 --> 06:03.880
What is it?

06:04.170 --> 06:08.330
A running list of known individuals 
identified as player killers.

06:08.330 --> 06:09.760
PKs?!

06:10.760 --> 06:15.600
<i>They took out lots of my friends 
and other people during the death game.</i>

06:15.600 --> 06:17.770
<i>They're deviants who kill for fun.</i>

06:20.350 --> 06:23.490
When players were first 
discovered in this world,

06:23.490 --> 06:28.860
Schnee was the one who insisted
that we look for PKs right away.

06:28.860 --> 06:30.030
She was?

06:30.030 --> 06:34.530
Sounds like she didn't tell you about that.

06:34.530 --> 06:37.960
No. This is the first I've heard 
of other players, too.

06:38.290 --> 06:43.790
I see. If I may say so, 
as your friend's follower,

06:43.790 --> 06:46.170
that's a clear act of betrayal.

06:47.130 --> 06:52.550
We mustn't deliberately withhold 
important information from our masters.

06:53.050 --> 06:57.020
She may be your follower, 
but she must be punished.

06:57.020 --> 07:00.770
No way. Schnee would never betray me.

07:01.150 --> 07:03.230
<i>Although, earlier...</i>

07:03.230 --> 07:05.440
<i>It's called Meow Land.</i>

07:05.440 --> 07:06.360
<i>Have you heard of it?</i>

07:06.360 --> 07:08.570
<i>No. I haven't the faintest idea.</i>

07:08.570 --> 07:10.570
I'm just kidding.

07:10.950 --> 07:12.490
Don't worry.

07:12.490 --> 07:17.870
Given Schnee's personality, I can't imagine 
she'd try to hurt you by hiding information.

07:17.870 --> 07:19.810
Come on, don't go yanking my chain.

07:19.810 --> 07:22.330
But you're right. Schnee would never
 do something like that.

07:22.330 --> 07:25.290
Well, that's enough reminiscing.

07:25.290 --> 07:27.710
I need to get ready for the flood as well.

07:27.710 --> 07:30.420
You do? Will you be fighting too?

07:30.420 --> 07:33.720
Oh, no. Valmer's safe with you around.

07:34.090 --> 07:36.010
I'll be preparing to stock up.

07:36.010 --> 07:38.970
There are plenty of materials 
to go around after a flood!

07:38.970 --> 07:42.730
<i>Come to think of it, this guy's 
backstory is that he loves money.</i>

07:46.940 --> 07:51.450
<i>I did some research on floods, 
and apparently a powerful individual</i>

07:51.450 --> 07:54.240
<i>has appeared amid 
low-level hordes a few times.</i>

07:55.120 --> 07:58.370
<i>The larger the flood, 
the more likely they are to show.</i>

07:58.370 --> 08:01.080
<i>So maybe, with this flood...</i>

08:01.080 --> 08:02.580
Oh, Shin.

08:02.580 --> 08:03.250
That you, Tiera?

08:03.250 --> 08:04.170
Shin!

08:04.170 --> 08:05.630
Whoa.

08:05.630 --> 08:07.540
I finally got to see you again.

08:07.540 --> 08:09.090
Good timing.

08:09.090 --> 08:10.590
Where's Schnee?

08:10.590 --> 08:12.510
Didn't she finish reporting to the lord?

08:12.510 --> 08:14.720
My master's very popular.

08:14.720 --> 08:16.890
They wouldn't let her leave so easily.

08:17.220 --> 08:20.280
I see. She's got it rough, too.

08:23.390 --> 08:26.260
Master, where are you going now?

08:26.260 --> 08:29.150
To meet with the chosen ones
 at the lord's castle.

08:29.780 --> 08:32.240
We'll be working together in battle.

08:33.820 --> 08:38.160
<i>Schnee returned in the middle of the night, 
so I never got to ask her about that.</i>

08:38.160 --> 08:40.790
<i>That's a clear act of betrayal.</i>

08:41.410 --> 08:42.740
Is something the matter?

08:42.740 --> 08:44.290
Nope. Let's get a move on.

08:48.840 --> 08:52.800
Schnee, thank you for coming.

08:53.170 --> 08:54.650
Allow me to introduce you.

08:54.650 --> 08:57.390
This is Shin, and this is Tiera.

08:57.390 --> 09:00.510
I am Tauro Yaxfair, lord of Valmer.

09:00.510 --> 09:01.930
A pleasure to meet you.

09:01.930 --> 09:05.440
We don't have much time 
before the flood arrives.

09:05.810 --> 09:12.440
The chosen ones will stand outside 
of Valmer with knights behind them.

09:12.750 --> 09:14.340
Once they are in firing range,

09:14.340 --> 09:18.200
our second squad, led by Schnee, will
 attack with magical area-of-effect skills.

09:18.700 --> 09:23.950
Our first squad and the knights 
will handle any monsters that get past you.

09:24.320 --> 09:29.080
I see. Then I shall instruct
 the knights personally.

09:29.080 --> 09:32.710
That'd be wonderful. We really appreciate it.

09:32.710 --> 09:34.210
Very well.

09:34.210 --> 09:36.510
They'll be training with my master?

09:36.510 --> 09:37.720
What's wrong, Tiera?

09:38.090 --> 09:43.100
Training with my master is hell. 
I feel sorry for them.

09:43.100 --> 09:46.390
Tiera, you'll be participating 
in the training as well.

09:46.730 --> 09:48.400
After all, teamwork is important.

09:48.400 --> 09:50.860
I-I'll do my best.

09:50.860 --> 09:52.730
Try not to die, Tiera.

09:57.260 --> 09:58.300
What's this?

09:59.050 --> 10:01.840
No sign of monsters?

10:01.840 --> 10:06.960
No. Monsters normally do appear that far out, 
but they've vanished completely.

10:07.470 --> 10:09.850
Probably an effect of the flood.

10:09.850 --> 10:13.610
As far as I know, there's no record
of this happening in the past.

10:13.610 --> 10:15.460
I've experienced it.

10:15.730 --> 10:19.590
The monsters in the area all but disappeared,

10:19.590 --> 10:22.220
then came surging forth like a black wave.

10:22.470 --> 10:25.060
<i>Of course there are no records of that.</i>

10:25.060 --> 10:27.480
<i>It was an in-game event.</i>

10:27.770 --> 10:30.400
<i>I'm glad Schnee played it off.</i>

10:30.400 --> 10:31.980
Do take care.

10:32.400 --> 10:37.110
It's possible there will be a powerful 
individual leading such a major flood.

10:38.610 --> 10:41.620
<i>In other words, the event boss.</i>

10:44.530 --> 10:45.870
I'm exhausted.

10:46.160 --> 10:49.250
Good job with your training. 
And thank you, Schnee.

10:49.250 --> 10:52.380
I appreciate you handling 
that conversation for me.

10:52.380 --> 10:53.750
But of course.

10:54.090 --> 10:57.050
By the way, Schnee, after I disappeared,

10:57.050 --> 11:00.470
did you ever use large-scale 
spells in guild battles?

11:00.470 --> 11:04.890
No. After all, I can handle most things 
with standard area-of-effect spells.

11:04.890 --> 11:08.230
So I should be careful 
about slinging mine around.

11:08.230 --> 11:11.310
Could you try using one 
during the opening strike?

11:11.310 --> 11:14.900
Yes. I'm sure that will be
 my only opportunity to use them.

11:15.270 --> 11:17.570
What are you up to next, Shin?

11:17.570 --> 11:23.410
Well, since I have the chance, 
I guess I'll update my disguises!

11:24.240 --> 11:25.780
I don't like the look on your face...

11:25.780 --> 11:27.790
<b>Moon Sanctum
</b>

11:34.500 --> 11:35.540
All done.

11:47.430 --> 11:51.340
Scouts have confirmed 
the presence of the monsters.

11:51.340 --> 11:54.520
Should a princess really be
taking part in a fight like this?

11:54.520 --> 11:56.190
A bit late for that old line, don't you think?

11:56.480 --> 11:59.690
It's a good opportunity 
to test the sword you gave me.

11:59.690 --> 12:02.610
I see. Then watch the rear.

12:02.610 --> 12:03.450
You got it.

12:09.040 --> 12:09.950
Shin.

12:10.540 --> 12:11.460
Schnee.

12:11.910 --> 12:15.080
There's something I'd like to discuss 
once this battle is over.

12:18.340 --> 12:20.170
They're here. Schnee.

12:20.170 --> 12:20.960
Yes.

12:22.520 --> 12:23.800
Blue Judge.

12:35.150 --> 12:37.060
Begin the offensive!

12:37.060 --> 12:37.980
Yeah!

12:37.980 --> 12:40.570
My master's incredible!

12:41.490 --> 12:42.990
But it's not over yet.

12:43.320 --> 12:45.820
Even after all that, they're still coming.

12:45.820 --> 12:48.490
This is no ordinary flood.

12:48.830 --> 12:50.870
<i>Schnee, can you fire off another?</i>

12:50.870 --> 12:55.500
<i>No. It seems I can't repeatedly 
use large-scale spells.</i>

12:55.500 --> 12:57.920
<i>Just like in the game.</i>

12:58.500 --> 13:02.630
<i>It's not exactly what we planned, 
but I'll kite the second wave of monsters.</i>

13:02.630 --> 13:03.880
<i>Understood.</i>

13:06.690 --> 13:08.350
Say hello to this.

13:08.350 --> 13:09.640
Amber Wave!

13:15.010 --> 13:15.950
Phoenix Sage!

13:22.780 --> 13:24.860
That should do for now.

13:24.860 --> 13:28.870
I'd like to save my best abilities 
for later, so the rest is up to you.

13:30.240 --> 13:31.440
Get them!

13:31.440 --> 13:33.950
Don't let your guard down 
until they've stopped breathing!

13:33.950 --> 13:34.790
Yeah!

13:40.380 --> 13:42.880
Wow, Tiera!

13:42.880 --> 13:46.720
Shin said he made some 
adjustments so I could use it,

13:46.720 --> 13:50.800
but he didn't tell me it'd be <i>this</i> powerful!

13:50.800 --> 13:51.760
Not bad.

13:59.310 --> 14:01.520
Follow Rionne's lead!

14:01.520 --> 14:02.650
Yeah!

14:08.320 --> 14:11.120
Looks like they're not all small fry.

14:17.710 --> 14:19.040
I need to help her!

14:20.170 --> 14:21.630
Tiera?

14:21.630 --> 14:24.050
I think I spent too much mana.

14:24.550 --> 14:26.590
Don't strain yourself.

14:27.080 --> 14:28.880
But at this rate...

14:30.590 --> 14:31.970
Sorry to keep you waiting.

14:34.100 --> 14:35.470
You...

14:35.470 --> 14:37.520
You have a letter of introduction.

14:37.520 --> 14:38.730
The name's Wilhelm.

14:38.730 --> 14:40.980
I'm here to save you, princess.

14:41.650 --> 14:42.860
It's that man!

14:43.360 --> 14:44.810
It's good to see you again.

14:45.400 --> 14:46.990
Lacia!

14:46.990 --> 14:49.990
Allow me to restore your mana.

14:50.280 --> 14:51.490
Let's go!

14:51.740 --> 14:53.030
Flashing Blossom!

14:53.530 --> 14:55.700
Full Moon Edge!

15:00.830 --> 15:02.420
Thank you.

15:02.420 --> 15:04.840
But what are you doing in Valmer?

15:04.840 --> 15:07.010
The guild received a request for assistance.

15:07.420 --> 15:10.010
Besides, after what she said...

15:10.230 --> 15:12.720
There are lots of monsters! They're in danger!

15:13.010 --> 15:15.220
Go help Shin!

15:15.500 --> 15:19.370
I doubt he's struggling, though.

15:22.900 --> 15:24.060
What's that?

15:26.480 --> 15:28.490
I'm finally up.

15:35.330 --> 15:36.530
Are you okay?

15:36.530 --> 15:38.080
Wh-Who are you?

15:38.080 --> 15:40.500
Who, me? Well...

15:41.120 --> 15:42.670
Call me Red.

15:42.670 --> 15:44.000
O-Okay.

15:44.540 --> 15:46.840
Sorry, but I need you to clear out.

15:46.840 --> 15:50.510
I can't use my abilities properly 
with you guys around.

15:50.510 --> 15:51.760
B-But...

15:51.760 --> 15:54.390
I might end up killing you, too.

15:55.010 --> 15:56.890
That's how this weapon works.

16:00.390 --> 16:01.980
Retreat!

16:01.980 --> 16:04.150
Just who is that guy?

16:07.440 --> 16:08.150
<i>Shin...</i>

16:08.820 --> 16:10.990
<i>That's a cursed weapon, isn't it?</i>

16:15.120 --> 16:16.910
Wh-What is that?

16:16.910 --> 16:21.370
A weapon that instantly slays—
no, consumes everything.

16:21.370 --> 16:23.710
He's a monster.

16:23.710 --> 16:25.540
Kill, kill!

16:25.830 --> 16:28.500
Kill, kill! Kill more!

16:28.500 --> 16:31.210
More, more, more!

16:31.210 --> 16:34.800
Oh, shut up. Cursed weapons are so noisy.

16:35.260 --> 16:40.270
This scythe is perfect for floods 
since it attracts enemy aggro, but...

16:41.140 --> 16:42.350
Found it.

16:45.910 --> 16:46.980
A demon.

16:47.480 --> 16:50.650
That's the event boss leading the flood.

16:58.830 --> 17:02.250
<i>A mind-affecting attack, huh? Too bad...</i>

17:02.770 --> 17:04.330
Limit Off.

17:12.050 --> 17:15.470
That won't work against a high human like me.

17:18.180 --> 17:20.970
<i>Shin, the monsters have been exterminated.</i>

17:21.310 --> 17:23.060
<i>We suffered zero casualties.</i>

17:23.060 --> 17:24.180
<i>Roger.</i>

17:28.650 --> 17:29.860
I want to go home.

17:29.860 --> 17:31.190
Same.

17:31.190 --> 17:35.240
I heard they wanted to reward those 
who fought admirably against the flood,

17:35.240 --> 17:37.280
but I didn't think they'd hold a ceremony.

17:37.280 --> 17:40.080
If that's the custom in Valmer,
we must endure it.

17:41.580 --> 17:44.410
Sorry to keep you waiting. Let's go.

17:44.870 --> 17:47.040
R-Right...

17:50.250 --> 17:53.300
<i>Stuff like this isn't my thing.</i>

17:54.210 --> 17:57.760
<i>Wilhelm and Lacia said they weren't 
interested and left already.</i>

17:59.800 --> 18:02.850
Kindly take my arms, ladies!

18:02.850 --> 18:04.140
How did that sound?

18:05.180 --> 18:07.390
That was so out of character!

18:07.390 --> 18:10.560
You should be glad you have 
a lovely lady on each arm today.

18:10.560 --> 18:13.650
I appreciate the escort.

18:18.320 --> 18:20.120
Everyone's looking at us.

18:20.120 --> 18:22.490
Yeah, I'll bet they are.

18:22.490 --> 18:24.580
Shall we move to the edge of the room?

18:24.580 --> 18:25.410
Yeah.

18:25.410 --> 18:28.000
Shin! You finally showed.

18:28.670 --> 18:29.710
Rionne.

18:31.750 --> 18:34.420
Shin, I've been wondering...

18:35.010 --> 18:37.510
Did something happen 
between you and the princess?

18:37.510 --> 18:39.800
N-Nothing happened.

18:39.800 --> 18:42.850
She's just interested 
in my equipment and spells.

18:42.850 --> 18:47.430
I see. I thought she'd made advances on you.

18:47.430 --> 18:48.890
Oh, uh...

18:48.890 --> 18:51.980
Shin, don't act so distant 
after making eye contact with me.

18:51.980 --> 18:55.320
People will stare if I'm with you.

18:55.320 --> 18:57.690
I don't mind at all.

18:57.690 --> 18:59.200
Very funny.

18:59.490 --> 19:01.820
Why are you acting so aloof?

19:01.820 --> 19:04.280
You've already proposed to me and everything.

19:04.280 --> 19:05.700
Hey! That wasn't...

19:05.700 --> 19:08.710
I'm joking. Forgive me for teasing you.

19:08.710 --> 19:10.760
I'm going to get some food.

19:10.760 --> 19:13.080
Don't let me get in your way.

19:13.840 --> 19:14.840
Schnee?

19:17.080 --> 19:22.430
Rionne, could you regale me with tales
of your heroism during the flood?

19:22.430 --> 19:23.470
Of course.

19:23.720 --> 19:27.420
Shin, could you go get a drink for Rionne?

19:27.420 --> 19:28.060
What?

19:28.640 --> 19:30.350
Oh, sure.

19:38.400 --> 19:39.990
It's a nice view.

19:39.990 --> 19:43.110
I'm sorry for stepping away.

19:43.740 --> 19:45.450
Were you jealous?

19:45.450 --> 19:50.210
Well, yes. After all, 
I'm not actually your fiancée.

19:50.210 --> 19:51.120
Schnee?

19:51.460 --> 19:54.630
Did Berett tell you?

19:54.930 --> 19:58.090
There are players besides me 
in this world, right?

19:58.760 --> 20:00.590
Player killers, too.

20:01.340 --> 20:03.340
Is that what you wanted to talk about?

20:03.340 --> 20:06.600
Yes. I'm sorry for hiding it from you.

20:06.600 --> 20:08.640
But I couldn't tell you.

20:09.020 --> 20:13.650
If you learned of the player killers, 
I thought you'd become <i>that</i> Shin again.

20:14.900 --> 20:18.020
The cold Shin who keeps everyone 
at arm's length.

20:19.690 --> 20:23.200
If I had as little sense of self as I did 
in the game, I could endure it.

20:23.950 --> 20:27.530
But now... Now, I don't think I could.

20:28.210 --> 20:30.080
I can't stop you.

20:30.080 --> 20:33.290
I can't replace her!

20:35.290 --> 20:41.550
Despite knowing that, there's a part 
of me that's glad she's gone.

20:42.010 --> 20:46.430
That thought maybe I could replace her.

20:46.430 --> 20:48.930
Maybe I could be your rock.

20:49.380 --> 20:52.010
So I... I...

20:57.900 --> 20:58.860
Sorry.

21:00.020 --> 21:01.690
Please don't apologize.

21:02.360 --> 21:04.360
Don't blame yourself too much.

21:05.360 --> 21:10.700
If I were in your shoes, 
I'd probably do the same.

21:10.700 --> 21:12.060
Shin...

21:12.060 --> 21:15.830
Listen. I'm really glad I found you, too.

21:16.620 --> 21:22.170
I thought it was finally all over when I beat 
the boss, but then I found myself here again.

21:22.170 --> 21:24.170
I didn't know anyone.

21:24.850 --> 21:28.090
My home felt like a stranger's house.

21:28.770 --> 21:34.730
So when you welcomed me back, 
I felt so relieved.

21:35.180 --> 21:37.900
You remembered me.

21:37.900 --> 21:39.480
Of course I did.

21:39.980 --> 21:42.570
Berett called it an act of betrayal,

21:43.150 --> 21:47.610
but I won't hold it against you or punish you.

21:48.070 --> 21:49.120
But I...

21:49.120 --> 21:51.870
I can't hear you. I've already made up my mind.

21:52.330 --> 21:54.790
I've made my decision.
I'll hear no objections.

21:56.620 --> 21:58.370
No more secrets between us.

21:59.830 --> 22:00.880
Okay.

22:01.340 --> 22:05.010
<i>Sorry, Schnee. This all started because I...</i>

22:05.010 --> 22:09.050
Um, Shin, may I ask you something?

22:09.050 --> 22:09.890
What is it?

22:13.350 --> 22:19.150
Do you still love Marino?

22:27.450 --> 22:31.240
Yeah. My feelings haven't changed.

22:32.370 --> 22:35.660
I see. I understand.

22:46.550 --> 22:50.180
I won't give up. I love you.

22:50.510 --> 22:53.760
I know you'll return to your world someday,

22:53.760 --> 22:56.930
but my feelings for you are real.

22:57.600 --> 23:00.100
W-We should head back inside.

23:02.730 --> 23:05.780
I wasn't expecting this...

23:07.690 --> 23:10.950
<i>I still don't know how to return to my world.</i>

23:12.530 --> 23:16.040
<i>I'm worried about the player killers
I crossed in the game, too.</i>

23:16.580 --> 23:22.580
<i>And if the friends I thought were dead 
are actually alive, then maybe...</i>

23:25.090 --> 23:25.960
Let's go.

23:26.750 --> 23:28.130
On to the next town!

23:34.970 --> 23:39.980
Thank you for watching
